{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N2"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 119, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty 0->3 edge with a conv adds a direct path and gives large gains, while replacing an existing skip or conv on that edge tends to hurt."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A residual 0->3 shortcut strongly helps conv-based cells but hurts conv-free skip or pool cells."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the residual skip on 0->3 is the most damaging removal, especially on ImageNet16-120."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 4 is absent, edge 5 is one of few remaining inputs to the output node, so removing it is much more harmful."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With fewer paths into node 3, deleting the direct input path removes a larger share of the information flow."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a new conv path into the output beats replacing an existing skip on edge 5."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv on an empty 1->3 edge adds capacity, whereas replacing a skip there can remove a useful shortcut."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pooling edge with a 3x3 conv adds the most learnable capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct 0->3 path, cutting 0->1 strands more of the